ur receipts</h2>${icon('receipt')}</div><p class="muted small">Save service details and a photo of each receipt on this device.</p><button class="button secondary" data-action="service">Log a service ${icon('arrow',16)}</button></div></div></div>`}
function drive(){let v=vehicle();if(!v)return intro('Mileage','Track your trips','Track personal and work driving.')+noVehicle();let trips=db.trips.filter(t=>t.vehicleId===v.id).sort((a,b)=>b.date.localeCompare(a.date));const business=trips.filter(t=>t.type==='business').reduce((a,t)=>a+Number(t.miles),0);const personal=trips.filter(t=>t.type!=='business').reduce((a,t)=>a+Number(t.miles),0);return intro('Mileage','Drive tracker',nativeMileageAvailable()?'Start GPS tracking or enable auto-detect before your drive. Tracking continues with the screen locked.':'GPS tracking is available while the app is open.',`<button class="button sm secondary" data-action="trip">${icon('plus',16)} Add trip</button>`)+`<div class="stack"><section class="panel"><div class="labelRow"><h2>Trip detection</h2><span class="status ${activeTrip||nativeMileageState.running?'good':'unknown'}" id="tripStatus">${activeTrip?'Recording':nativeMileageState.running?'Watching for driving':nativeMileageStarting?'Starting GPS':'Not recording'}</span></div><p class="muted small" style="margin:10px 0 20px">${activeTrip?(nativeMileageAvailable()?'GPS tracking stays active with the screen locked. Finish the trip to save the estimated miles.':'Keep PitNudge open while driving. Distance updates when accurate GPS readings arrive.'):(nativeMileageState.running?'Waiting for vehicle movement. A persistent Android notification lets you stop tracking.':nativeMileageAvailable()?'Turn on auto-detect before leaving, then you can lock your phone. Or start a trip manually.':'Enable automatic detection to watch for driving while the app is open, or start a trip manually.')}</p><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap"><label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="autoDetect" ${db.autoDetect?'checked':''}/> ${nativeMileageAvailable()?'Auto-detect driving with screen locked':'Auto-detect driving while open'}</label><span class="topTip">${icon('pin',14)} GPS access required</span></div>
       <label class="toggle space" style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:10px"><input type="checkbox" id="saveRouteMaps" ${db.saveRouteMaps?'checked':''}/><span><strong>Save trip route maps</strong><span class="small muted" style="display:block;font-weight:400">Optional: record map points for new trips. Routes are saved with your trip history and included in your optional cloud backup. You can remove a route later.</span></span></label>
       <div class="resultCard space"><div><div class="statLabel">Current trip</div><div class="valueLarge metric" id="liveMiles">${activeTrip?miles(activeTrip.miles):'0'} <span style="font-size:14px">mi</span></div><div class="small muted" id="liveKind">${activeTrip?`Recording for ${esc(vehicleName(db.vehicles.find(x=>x.id===activeTrip.vehicleId)))}`:(nativeMileageState.running?esc(nativeMileageState.message||'Watching for driving'):'No trip in progress')}</div></div><div>${icon('drive',38)}</div></div><div class="actions space"><button class="button" data-action="${activeTrip?'stopTrip':'startTrip'}">${icon(activeTrip?'check':'drive',18)} ${activeTrip?'Finish trip':nativeMileageState.running?'Stop monitoring':'Start GPS trip'}</button>${activeTrip?'<button class="button ghost" data-action="cancelTrip">Discard trip</button>':''}${activeTrip&&Array.isArray(activeTrip.route)&&activeTrip.route.length>1?'<button class="button secondary" data-action="viewLiveRoute">View live map</button>':''}</div>${activeTrip?`<div class="space"><label class="field">Trip category<select id="liveCategory"><option value="personal" ${activeTrip.type==='personal'?'selected':''}>Personal</option><option value="business" ${activeTrip.type==='business'?'selected':''}>Business (DoorDash, work, etc.)</option></select></label></div>`:''}</section><div class="note"><strong>GPS estimates:</strong> In the Android app, enable tracking <em>while PitNudge is open</em>; then your phone can lock while a visible tracking notification is running. Auto-detect watches for driving only after you turn it on, stops a trip after about 3 minutes stationary, and saves completed trips when you reopen PitNudge. This is not 24/7 always-on detection; GPS may miss miles indoors or without signal. Turn on <strong>Save trip route maps</strong> to compare your route with the distance your car reports. Earlier trips cannot be mapped because they did not record coordinates. Check your dashboard odometer periodically.</div><div class="grid2"><div class="panel"><div class="statLabel">Business miles logged</div><div class="statNum metric">${miles(business)}</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="statLabel">Personal miles logged</div><div class="statNum metric">${miles(personal)}</div></div></div><section class="panel"><div class="panelHead"><h2>Recent trips</h2><button class="button sm ghost" data-action="trip">${icon('plus',14)} Manual trip</button></div>${trips.length?trips.slice(0,15).map(t=>`<div class="record"><div><div style="font-weight:750">${miles(t.miles)} miles <span class="chip">${t.type==='business'?'Business':'Personal'}</span></div><div class="small muted">${humanDate(t.date)} · ${t.source==='gps'?'GPS estimate':'Manual entry'}${t.note?' · '+esc(t.note):''}</div></div><div class="actions">${Array.isArray(t.route)&&t.route.length>1?`<button class="button sm secondary" data-action="viewTripRoute" data-id="${t.id}">${icon('pin',14)} View map</button>`:''}<button class="button sm secondary" data-action="editTrip" data-id="${t.id}">Edit</button><button class="button sm ghost" data-action="deleteTrip" data-id="${t.id}" aria-label="Delete trip">${icon('trash',16)}</button></div></div>`).join(''):'<div class="empty"><p>No trips recorded yet. Start GPS tracking or add your first drive manually.</p></div>'}</section></div>`}
function service(){let v=vehicle();if(!v)return intro('Care schedule','Maintenance','See what your vehicle needs next.')+noVehicle();let s=Object.keys(DEFAULTS).map(k=>serviceInfo(v,k)).sort((a,b)=>severity[a.status]-severity[b.status]);return intro('Vehicle care','Maintenance','Default intervals are examples only. Adjust each reminder to your owner’s manual.',`<button class="button sm" data-action="service">${icon('plus',16)} Log service</button>`)+`<div class="stack"><div class="banner"><strong>Vehicle-specific advice:</strong> Recommended service timing varies by car, oil type, driving conditions, and manufacturer. These starter reminders are customizable and are not official service schedules.</div><section class="panel"><div class="panelHead"><h2>${esc(vehicleName(v))}</h2><span class="topTip">${miles(v.mileage)} mi</span></div>${s.map(x=>serviceTile(x)).join('')}</section><section class="panel"><div class="panelHead"><h2>DIY help</h2>${icon('book')}</div><p class="muted small">Basic owner checklists, plus a quick way to find local professional help.</p><div class="actions"><button class="button secondary" data-action="diy">See DIY basics</button><button class="button ghost" data-page="shops">Find a mechanic</button></div></section></div>`}
function shopLink(category){let queries={mechanic:'auto repair shops near me',oil:'oil change near me',tires:'tire shops near me',brakes:'brake repair shops near me',battery:'car battery replacement near me',towing:'auto towing near me'};return 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query='+encodeURIComponent(queries[category]||queries.mechanic)}
function shops(){return intro('Help near you','Find a mechanic','Search live shop listings, ratings, hours, and directions in Google Maps.')+`<div class="stack"><section class="shopPanel"><div class="mapArtwork" role="img" aria-label="Decorative illustration of a map, not live mechanic locations"><span class="mapPin one">📍</span><span class="mapPin two">📍</span><span class="mapPin three">📍</span><span class="mapCaption">Illustration · not live locations</span></div><h2 style="margin:0 0 7px">Need someone to fix it?</h2><p class="muted small" style="margin:0 0 18px">Open current nearby results with real shop details. You'll be able to call, check reviews, and get directions there.</p><a class="button" href="${shopLink('mechanic')}" rel="noopener noreferrer">${icon('pin',17)} Find mechanics near me</a></section><div class="grid2">${[['oil','Oil changes','droplet'],['tires','Tires & rotations','rotate'],['brakes','Brakes','shield'],['battery','Batteries','zap'],['towing','Towing','car']].map(([key,label,ico])=>`<a class="resultCard" style="text-decoration:none;color:var(--text)" href="${shopLink(key)}" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px">${icon(ico,21)} <strong>${label}</strong></span>${icon('arrow',17)}</a>`).join('')}</div><div class="note">PitNudge currently opens live search results in Google Maps; it does not yet display or verify individual mechanics inside the app. A built-in shop map could be added later.</div></div>`}
function more(){return intro('Your vehicle hub','More tools','Keep your vehicles, receipts, and trip records organized.')+`<div class="tabline">${[['account','My account'],['garage','My garage'],['records','Receipts & costs'],['taxes','Tax records'],['settings','Settings']].map(([k,t])=>`<button class="pill ${moreTab===k?'selected':''}" data-more="${k}">${t}</button>`).join('')}</div>`+({account:accountSection,garage:garageSection,records:recordsSection,taxes:taxSection,settings:settingsSection}[moreTab]||accountSection)()}
// Native authentication is disabled until an independent Firebase project is configured.
// There are no passwords/tokens in the local HTML or browser storage.
let account={configured:false,signedIn:false,uid:null,email:null,provider:null,syncActive:false,
  serverSnapshot:null,cloudMessage:'Not connected',syncedAt:null};
const cloudBridge=()=>window.NativePitNudge;
function accountSection(){
  const configured=account.configured;
  const hasAccount=account.signedIn;
  let name=account.email||'Your account';
  let cloudStatus=account.syncActive?'Cloud sync enabled':account.cloudMessage;
  return `<div class="stack">
  <section class="panel"><div class="panelHead"><h2>${icon('car',19)} PitNudge account</h2><span class="status ${hasAccount?'good':'unknown'}">${hasAccount?'Signed in':'Guest mode'}</span></div>
    ${hasAccount?`<p><strong>${esc(name)}</strong></p><p class="muted small">Your local garage is on this phone. Cloud backup status: <strong>${esc(cloudStatus)}</strong>.</p>
    <div class="actions space"><button class="button secondary" data-action="cloudSave">Back up this phone</button><button class="button ghost" data-action="cloudRestore">Restore cloud backup</button><button class="button ghost" data-action="accountLogout">Sign out</button></div>`:
    `<p class="muted">Sign in to save vehicle records under your own account and restore them when you switch phones.</p>
    <div class="actions space"><button class="button" data-action="googleLogin" ${!configured?'disabled':''}>Continue with Google</button><button class="button secondary" data-action="appleLogin" ${!configured?'disabled':''}>Continue with Apple</button></div>
    ${!configured?`<p class="small amber space">Account sign-in is not activated yet. PitNudge still works offline, and your garage stays on this phone until we finish secure cloud setup.</p>`:
    `<p class="small muted space">Your information stays local until you sign in and select cloud backup.</p>`}`}
  </section>
  <section class="panel"><h2>What your account will save</h2><p class="muted small">Vehicles and odometer readings, maintenance records and schedules, trip logs, and service expenses. Receipt photos are included only while within current cloud document limits; larger photo backups will need separate secure image storage.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Each account is stored separately. If PitNudge finds records on both your phone and in the cloud, it will ask which copy to use instead of deleting either silently.</p>
    <div class="actions space"><button class="button secondary" data-action="backup">Save a local backup</button><button class="button ghost" data-more="settings">Backup settings</button></div>
  </section>
  </div>`;
}
window.PitNudgeAccount={
  onAuthState(encoded){
    try{const a=JSON.parse(encoded); account.configured=!!a.configured;account.uid=a.uid||null;
      account.signedIn=!!a.uid;account.email=a.email||null;account.provider=a.provider||null;
      account.syncActive=false;account.cloudMessage=a.uid?'Checking cloud backup…':'Not connected';
      if(!a.uid) account.serverSnaps